<Legal title="Probe Cloud (preview)" description="Probe Cloud is a hosted report service for FlutterProbe, in preview. What exists today, what is planned, and how to become a design partner.">
  <h1>Probe Cloud (preview)</h1>
  <p>Probe Cloud is a hosted place to keep your FlutterProbe test reports. It is a preview, not generally available, and plan details are not final. The CLI, agent and local tools remain free.</p>

  <h2>What exists today</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>probe test --upload-report</code> sends a run report to a Probe Cloud endpoint, with CI details (provider, branch, commit) and an optional <code>--upload-label</code>.</li>
    <li><code>--upload-dry-run</code> prints exactly what would be sent, so you can inspect it before anything leaves your machine.</li>
    <li>The payload is scrubbed before sending: paths are made relative, secret-looking values are redacted, and screenshots and device identifiers are left out. Uploads are capped at 1 MiB and 5,000 results.</li>
    <li>JUnit and JSON reports for any CI system, with no account needed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is planned</h2>
  <p>A dashboard for run history and trends, shared report links for your team, and notifications. These are planned, not built, and may change.</p>

  <h2>Design partners</h2>
  <p>We are looking for the first 10 Flutter teams. During the beta it is free, and when paid plans launch you get 50% off for life. In return we ask for honest feedback after you use it on a real project. The beta may change or end.</p>
  <p><a href="mailto:support@alphawavesystems.com?subject=Probe%20Cloud%20design%20partner">Apply by email</a>, or <a href="https://github.com/AlphaWaveSystems/flutter-probe/issues/new?title=Probe%20Cloud%20design%20partner">open a public GitHub issue</a>. See <a href="/pricing/#design-partners">pricing</a>, the <a href="/terms/">terms</a> and the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</Legal>
